  "limits": [
    "Attests the exact clean integration HEAD and unchanged target captured by this run; it never installs, merges, pushes or authorizes a different tree.",
    "Retains the original M0 contract and baseline. Reviewed assertion/harness deltas require their own externally pinned digest; no skipped, cancelled, TODO or reduced-count suite can pass.",
    "Linux evidence covers the explicitly recorded Node 22 and Node 26 patches in pinned Linux/arm64 containers with local HTTPS/WSS proxy fixtures; it does not establish a public VPS, DNS, multi-host or production reverse-proxy deployment.",
    "Signed desktop fixtures use the supplied matching packaged app and disposable data. Codesign integrity is checked; publisher authenticity and notarization are not claimed.",
    "Workload budgets are observed on the recorded machine and filesystem, with serial gate commands. They are not universal capacity or latency guarantees.",
    "Semantic model quality, physical keyboard/IME/accessibility interaction, power-loss durability, unsupported operating systems and untested deployment configurations remain outside this automated evidence.",
    "Composed scenarios repeat two real host Chromium contexts, a shipped CLI stream and a raw writer locally and against a pinned Linux backend; workload human actors are protocol drivers rather than browser UI users.",
    "Upgrade evidence replaces runtimes only on disposable roots created with the frozen old runtime and an extracted pinned candidate package; it does not publish a release or install over a real user installation."
  ],
